  "dimensions": [
    {
      "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#dimension_8dcb73c4",
      "@type": "OverallIntent",
      "instance_name": "overallintent_instance",
      "label": "the overallintent",
      "description": "meme-id: meme_image; hasOverallIntent: Hateful; overall-intent-description: The image depicts a scene of devastation and chaos, with a man in the foreground raising his arm in apparent anger or protest while surrounded by the wreckage of a car and other people. The overlaid text reads: 'how dare people make fun of our peaceful religion.' This juxtaposition is intentionally provocative and inflammatory. The meme uses the visual of a violent or traumatic event — likely a car bombing or explosion — to frame a religious group as being 'peaceful,' while simultaneously implying that outsiders are mocking them. This is a hateful construction because it weaponizes suffering and destruction to defend a religious identity, suggesting that the violence depicted is somehow justified or connected to the 'peaceful' nature of the religion being defended. It also implies that the perpetrators of the violence are outsiders mocking the religion, which is a dangerous and false narrative. The meme is designed to provoke strong emotional reactions and to delegitimize criticism of the religion by equating it with violence, thereby fostering hostility toward those who question or criticize it. The overall intent is to incite hatred or fear toward critics of the religion by associating them with the violence depicted, while simultaneously portraying the religion as victimized and peaceful — a dangerous and misleading framing that can fuel further division and violence.",
      "belongsToAnalysis": {
        "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#analysis_2f0867bd"
      },
      "extractionMethod": "llm_extraction_huggingface"
    },
